<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

        <title>[[title]] - Privacy Policy</title>

        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/styles.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/privacy.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <%view navbar %>
        <div id="main-content">
            <div id="privacy-title-text">[[title]] Privacy Policy</div>
            <hr>
            <div id="privacy-text">
                You do not have privacy here. It is the internet after all.
                <br />
                <strong>what is being collected about me?</strong><br>
                In the access log: Your <strong>IP address, User agent, and any paths you have visited on the website</strong><br>
                In the server session storage: Your <strong>User Id</strong><br />

                <strong>what about cookies?</strong> <br />
                <strong>SessionId</strong> - Stores the token so you don't have to type your password on every single page<br />

                That is it.
            </div>
        </div>
        <%view footer %>
    </body>
</html>
